# 5. EC2-B Security Group

Name:

```text
saa-lab-1-b
```

ID:

```text
sg-0example2
```

Final intended inbound rules:

| Protocol | Port | Source                                 | Purpose                                         |
| -------- | ---: | -------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
| TCP      |   80 | `saa-lab-1-a` (`sg-0example1`) | Allow HTTP from EC2-A                           |
| TCP      |   22 | EICE SG (`sg-0example3`)       | Allow SSH through EC2 Instance Connect Endpoint |

Outbound:

```text
All traffic → 0.0.0.0/0
```

The important rule is:

```text
TCP 80
Source = EC2-A Security Group
```

NOT:

```text
0.0.0.0/0
```

and NOT:

```text
172.31.26.167/32
```

The Security Group reference is the important SAA concept.

