# 13. First HTTP Test

Before installing a web server, we tested:

```bash
curl -v --connect-timeout 5 http://172.31.16.13:80
```

The result was:

```text
Connection refused
```

This was different from a timeout.

### Meaning

The network path was reachable, but nothing was listening on TCP port 80.

This distinction is useful when troubleshooting:

```text
TIMEOUT
    ↓
Often network/security/routing problem

CONNECTION REFUSED
    ↓
Host is reachable,
but application/service is not listening
```

