# 15. Why EC2-B Could Not Reach the Internet

EC2-B had:

```text
172.31.16.13
```

but no public IPv4 address.

It did have a default route:

```text
default via 172.31.16.1 dev ens5
```

and the VPC local route.

However, having a default route does not automatically mean an instance has Internet access.

For private instances to reach the Internet, AWS normally requires an appropriate egress design, such as:

```text
Private EC2
    ↓
NAT Gateway
    ↓
Internet Gateway
    ↓
Internet
```

A NAT Gateway would be unnecessary for this lab.

Therefore, instead of modifying the architecture just to install Nginx, we used Python's built-in HTTP server.

