# 18. Final Security Group Experiment

After removing the temporary SSH rule from EC2-B, we tested both ports from EC2-A.

### Port 22

```bash
nc -vz -w 5 172.31.16.13 22
```

Result:

```text
nc: connect to 172.31.16.13 port 22 timed out
```

Therefore:

```text
EC2-A → EC2-B :22
❌ BLOCKED
```

### Port 80

```bash
curl http://172.31.16.13
```

Result:

```text
HTTP/1.0 200 OK
Server: SimpleHTTP/0.6 Python/3.13.5
```

Therefore:

```text
EC2-A → EC2-B :80
✅ ALLOWED
```

This was the core experiment.

